# Jak 1: each kind of settings row by the pointer (LIST-0.1.3 item 1), with JAKVR_POINTER_TRACE=1, on a copy of the
# settings (C:\JakQuest\sim\gkcfg-ptrset) since it changes them. Aims as jak1_ptr_settings_cal.sim found them (sim b75):
# pitch atan((0.35 + (0.5 - v) * 1.26) / 1.3) with v = y / 224, yaw atan((0.2 - (u - 0.5) * 1.68) / 1.3) with u = x / 512
# (a row is 370 wide from x 17: its middle x 202 is yaw 16.2; x 110 is 27.6, x 300 is 2.45, x 80 is 30.9, x 330 is -1.9,
# x 360 is -6.2, x 200 is 16.45). Game Options shows 6 of its 10 rows from y 40, 25 high: the second (Play hints) at
# pitch 22.7, the fifth (Language) at 5.4; the hand at rest (pitch 0) points at the sixth.
# - Game Options opened with the hand at rest: its first row stays chosen and the page does not move (b75: it moved on
#   by itself to Back; build 61), pictures at once and after 3 s.
# - Play hints (On / Off): the dot onto it and a click (Cross: the row is being changed), the dot onto the right half
#   (Off, without a click), a click there (done); a click on the row again, the dot onto the left half (On), a click.
# - Language (a list): a click (being changed), a click on its right third (a step right), on its left third (a step
#   left, back), in its middle (done).
# - B back, the stick down to Sound Options, A; SFX volume (a slider; the page's 4 rows from y 65) at pitch 22.7: a click (being changed), the trigger
#   held on the bar at x 200 (the bar takes the dot: about half), the hand turned right to x 300 while held (about 88
#   in 100), let go, a click off the bar at x 360 (done).
